'' A procedure type's parameters take the byref default, and a typedef to an undefined
'' type is a forward reference. Both names measured against fbc's object symbols.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-mangle tests/mangle/src/procptr-param-byref.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: _Z2G1PFvR4UDT1E
'' EXPECT-OUT: _Z2G1PFvR8FWDREF1_E
'' EXPECT-OUT: _Z2G1PFvR8FWDREF2_E
'' EXPECT-OUT: _Z2G1PFvR8FBSTRINGE
'' EXPECT-OUT: _Z2G1PFviE
'' An explicit BYVAL is not the default and is a different type.
'' EXPECT-OUT: _Z2G1PFv4UDT1E
'' EXPECT-NOT: _Z2G1PFvvE
'' The RANK is part of the FBARRAY template's name, on a real parameter...
'' EXPECT-OUT: _Z2K1R7FBARRAYIu7INTEGERE
'' EXPECT-OUT: _Z2K2R8FBARRAY1Iu7INTEGERE
'' EXPECT-OUT: _Z2K3R8FBARRAY2Iu7INTEGERE
'' ...and inside a procedure type, where the parameter used to be dropped.
'' EXPECT-OUT: _Z2M1PFvR7FBARRAYIu7INTEGEREE
'' EXPECT-OUT: _Z2M2PFvR8FBARRAY1Iu7INTEGEREE
'' EXPECT-OUT: _Z2M3PFvR8FBARRAY2Iu7INTEGEREE
'' An ellipsis in a procedure type is 'z' and makes a different type.
'' EXPECT-OUT: _Z2N1PFvu7INTEGERE
'' EXPECT-OUT: _Z2N2PFvu7INTEGERzE
'' GOLDEN: expected/procptr-param-byref.out
